course: dictionary
lesson: 213
title: Algae: tiny living plants of water
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: An alga is a simple living thing that is a bit like a plant, but it has no roots, stems, leaves or flowers. It grows in water or damp places and makes its food from sunlight. We usually say algae, which means more than one alga.
explain: «Green algae grow in a sloth's fur and help to hide it among the leaves.» Algae are living on something else here, and they are green like the leaves around the sloth. The clues are "green" and "grow", so you can work out that algae are the green things growing there.
explain: Algae are not just a nuisance. They are the start of many water food chains, and they make much of the world's oxygen. But too many algae can turn a pond green and harm fish. Scientists call this an «algal bloom».
fact: An alga is a simple living thing that makes its food from sunlight.
fact: Algae have no roots, stems, leaves or flowers.
fact: The plural of alga is algae.
fact: «Algae» can be found in ponds, fish tanks and on rocks, and they can make these slippery.
fact: An «algal bloom» is a large growth of algae that can harm fish.
exercise: «Green turtles visit cleaning stations where fish pick algae off their shells.» What are algae in this sentence? | *Tiny plant-like living things growing on the shell | Small fish that live inside the shell | Hard shells on the sea floor | Sea birds that eat turtles
exercise: What does an alga use to make its food? | Soil from the ground | Dust from the air | Other fish | *Sunlight
exercise: Which word is the plural of alga? | algal | *algae | alga's | algoes
test: «Too much algae can turn a pond green and harm fish.» What is an «algal bloom»? | A cleaning station for turtles | A type of fish that eats algae | A flower that opens on a pond | *A large growth of algae that can harm fish
test: In everyday life, algae can make rocks, pools and fish tanks what? | Sparkly like glass | Warm and dry | *Slippery | Hard as iron
exam: Which description fits an alga best? | *A simple plant-like living thing with no roots, stems, leaves or flowers | A fish that eats plants | A tree with roots, stems and leaves | A rock that grows in water
